{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Like the tower of David</b><br>Talpiyyot. Some say: for hanging swords, as in 'and it has two' — and they are five words. Others say that the tav is in place of alef, and it is from מלפנו מבהמות ארץ. The precise analysts said that the alef is missing and the tav is added, like תלבושת, and the matter is to teach wayfarers by its great height:" "Shields of the mighty. Like '[they brandished the arrows], they filled the quivers' — and they are the arrow-cases:" "<b>This time, the third</b><br>[Your neck.] The commanders of the army:"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ולה שתי פיות' (and it has two [edges?]) and the count 'five words' are cryptic; translated literally without resolution. The root citation מלפנו מבהמות ארץ (Job 35:11) is retained in Hebrew as Ibn Ezra quotes it.", 1 "The bracketed phrase הברו החצים appears corrupt or abbreviated; translated hyper-literally.", 2 "The bracketed lemma 'צוארך' (your neck) indicates Ibn Ezra is resuming discussion of the same word from earlier in the passage."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:16.550668724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}